  "_comment": [
    "The Monster: which heads of model.txt move together, the joint each part turns about, and its poses.",
    "Coordinates are the model's once centred on its feet and turned to face +z (its right hand on -x).",
    "A part turns [pitch, yaw, roll] degrees about its pivot (pitch > 0 bends forward) and carries its children.",
    "A pose is drawn from its anchor: T(anchor) * yaw * T(lift) * tilt. 'place' says what the anchor is in the",
    "world: ground (the floor it stands on), ceiling (the underside of the block above), block (the top of",
    "the block it lies on), air (a point in the air) or action (only played once it has been seen).",
    "'at' and 'yaw' only place it round the viewer's player, who stands at 'player' facing +z (or at the",
    "pose's own 'player': x, y, z, yaw); in the game the anchor is found in the world and it faces the player.",
    "'eyes' and 'palm' are points of the model the game aims with: where it looks from, and the hand it",
    "covers the player's view with."
  ],
